  "id": "COMPOUND:25832 - PROTEIN:6304",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a direct relationship between Ergosta-4,24(28)-dien-3-one and Microtubule-associated protein 1B, mediated through the Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. This compound is identified as a target of multiple metabolites, including two structurally distinct compounds that both target the same protein. The shared target of these metabolites implies a potential mechanism of action involving the SDR family member 9, which may play a role in modulating microtubule dynamics through interactions with the protein. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the same target suggests that Ergosta-4,24(28)-dien-3-one may influence Microtubule-associated protein 1B through a common intermediary, possibly by altering the activity or stability of the SDR family member 9. This integrated evidence highlights a potential role for Ergosta-4,24(28)-dien-3-one in regulating microtubule-associated processes via this protein.",
